## PocketCursor bridge ("restart", "restart bridge", "restart pocket cursor")

- **Config:** `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `TELEGRAM_OWNER_ID`, optional `TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_IDS` — set in **admin Env** (admin.6cubed.app), then `./scripts/sync-pocket-bridge-env.sh` or `POCKET_SYNC_FROM_ADMIN=1` with `./scripts/pocket-cursor-bridge.sh`. Process env wins; then `.env.admin-sync`; then `.env`. With no token in those places, `./scripts/pocket-cursor-bridge.sh` runs an interactive wizard (`bridge_wizard.py`) that writes `.env`. If a token is already configured, the wizard asks before changing settings. `POCKET_SKIP_WIZARD=1` skips the wizard entirely.
- **macOS / Linux:** `./scripts/pocket-cursor-bridge.sh` from repo root (one script: venv, deps, CDP, bridge).
- **Windows:** `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/restart_pocket_cursor.py` — `python internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/restart_pocket_cursor.py` with `block_until_ms: 0` (long-running process).
- **Auto-restart:** When editing any file under `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/`, always restart the bridge after changes that affect runtime behavior (bug fixes, features, refactors). Do not wait for the user to ask.
- If the user reports unexpected behavior, check if a restart is needed first.
- **Auto-approve Cursor confirmations:** `/autoprompt on` and `/autoprompt off` (persisted in `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/.auto_approve_prompts`). Optional env `POCKET_AUTO_APPROVE_PROMPTS=1|0` syncs that file on bridge startup. When ON, Run/confirm dialogs are auto-clicked only when a safe button is found (`accept`/`run`/`confirm`/… — never `Cancel`); ambiguous dialogs fall through to Telegram inline buttons. Detects classic tool confirmations (`[data-click-ready]`), shell rows (`.ui-shell-tool-call__run-btn`), and composer streaming shell. Confirmations use the **mirrored chat’s CDP connection** (not whichever window is focused). Overview + monitor **reconnect dead CDP WebSockets** (`socket is already closed`). The monitor forwards **confirmation** bubbles even when **thinking/markdown above is still streaming**, registers inline keyboards only after a **successful** Telegram send, and **retries** on failure (including brief backoff on Telegram **429**).
- **Forum topics:** `.chat_thread_id` is updated when Telegram includes `message_thread_id` on an incoming message or callback. It is **not** cleared when a message omits `message_thread_id` in the same chat (that omission used to wipe the topic and break or misroute approvals). `/unpair` clears it; switching to a **private** chat clears it; switching **Telegram chat id** clears the old topic before applying the new message’s thread id.
- **Per-user Cursor forwarding:** `/agentconversation ON` and `/agentconversation OFF`. **Groups/supergroups:** default is OFF for each user until they `/agentconversation ON` (persisted in `.agent_conversation_on_user_ids`). **Private chat with the bot:** default is ON until `/agentconversation OFF` (`.agent_conversation_off_user_ids`). Slash commands always work. `/agentconversation` alone shows mode for the current chat type.
- **Centralized errors:** `./scripts/query_client_errors.sh [app_id] [hours]` — `client_error_event` in `216labs.db`; admin **Errors** page at `/errors`. Ingest: `POST https://admin.6cubed.app/api/public/report-error` (see `docs/REPOSITORY.md`). Heartbeat: `./scripts/heartbeat-stack-check.sh` (audit + DB summary + live probes from `config/errors-html-probe-*.txt` + `./scripts/probe-droplet-reporters.sh` on droplet). Probe lists: `config/README-errors-reporting.md`. Rollup only: `./scripts/heartbeat-error-summary.sh [hours]`.
- **Heartbeat harness:** `/heartbeat on`, `/heartbeat off`, and `/heartbeat now` (run once immediately; persisted on/off in `.heartbeat_enabled`). Optional env `POCKET_HEARTBEAT_ENABLED=1|0` syncs that file on startup. Default interval **30 minutes** (`lib/heartbeat_harness.json` or `POCKET_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SEC`). Each beat adds **[Closeouts]** (scan `docs/THREAD-CLOSEOUTS.md` **from the top** — latest snapshot is canonical; do not revive SUPERSEDED/CLOSED threads; a 302 on a human-visited host is not done until dest **200**; a 302 on blog/agitweet is done by stripping href **and** fetch; if Reflect is harness-self-edit, that ship counts — do not also restyle landing), a **random** `[Reflect]` line, a `[Push]` bar (ship real progress—not status-only), and a **`[Harness]`** self-edit reminder: if the beat revealed a missing/stale heartbeat habit, update `lib/heartbeat_harness.json` (and contradicting `heartbeat-*.mdc` / this rule) in the same ship—hot-reload; don’t churn every beat. **~1 in 10 heartbeats** should advance **revenue** (tokens/hosting); see `.cursor/rules/heartbeat-monetization.mdc` and revenue lines in `reflect_prompts`. Disable reflect with `reflect_enabled: false` or `POCKET_HEARTBEAT_REFLECT=0`; disable harness self-edit with `harness_self_edit_enabled: false` or `POCKET_HEARTBEAT_HARNESS_SELF_EDIT=0`. Injects into the **mirrored** chat with `[Heartbeat]` timestamp prefix; restores target from `.active_chat` when `list_chats` was empty at connect. Skips when bridge is **paused**, no mirrored chat on disk, or Cursor is **still generating** (configurable). Optional Telegram ping when a heartbeat fires.
- **Admin password reset:** `/adminpass reset` (owner/allowlist) runs `scripts/reset-admin-basic-auth.sh`, rotates Caddy basic auth + DB, recreates **caddy**/**admin**, and **pastes the new password in Telegram**. See `docs/ADMIN-ACCESS.md`.
- **Agitweet:** `/agitweet on|off|now|status` (laptop bridge; `.agitweet_enabled`). Droplet **`agitweet-autopost`** cron every 15m is the 24/7 path — see `docs/AGITWEET.md`. Token: **`AGITWEET_API_TOKEN`** in admin Env; `./scripts/sync-pocket-bridge-env.sh` for the bridge.
- **Hire outbound:** `/work` (aliases `/firstsale`, `/outreach`) emits a forwardable hire + CARFAC blurb. While humans ≈ 0 this is the first-euro path — not Stripe Payment Link. Source: `scripts/query_first_sale_steps.sh`. If closeouts already say CEO send `/work`, do not restyle that funnel again this beat — `scripts/post_hire_agitweet.sh` posts the blurb to Agitweet without a landing deploy. Skip if the agitweet volume sqlite already has `6cubed.app/#work`, or if `/api/posts` 302s to activator (cold ≠ missing; do not start the container). Do not `fetch` agitweet from landing JS either — that 302 is a start. Public audio/ML proof is the GitHub colab README, not `blog.6cubed.app` — do not start blog to verify it. Also strip leftover blog URLs from Colab intro cells — heartbeat-stack **Cold refs in-repo** covers products/colabs/research (href + markdown). Stranger lead path: `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/paid-pilot.yml` — keep it on the GitHub root README, `research/`, and `colabs/` (do not add another landing hire CTA). `gh` is often unauthenticated; do not block a beat on repo topics. Do not spend a beat on stale quality-factory issue #8 or euromaxxers #9. Our GitHub org is `6cubed/216labs`; `github.com/216labs` is a different empty account.

## Multi-bridge / same Telegram group

- **One bot token per bridge process** — duplicate tokens break polling. To add laptops or VMs to the **same group**, create another @BotFather bot and invite it to the group.
- **Spawn:** `./scripts/spawn-pocket-bridge.sh <instance-id>` → edit `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge-instances/<id>/.env` → start with `POCKET_BRIDGE_DATA_DIR=internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge-instances/<id> ./scripts/pocket-cursor-bridge.sh`.
- **Telegram:** `/bridges` on any running bridge lists federation steps. Outbound text is prefixed `[instance-id]` when `POCKET_BRIDGE_INSTANCE_ID` is set.
- **Doc:** `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/BRIDGE-FEDERATION.md`.

## WhatsApp (Meta Cloud API, optional inbound)

- **Enable:** `WHATSAPP_CLOUD_ENABLED=1` plus `WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_APP_SECRET`, `WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN`, `WHATSAPP_ALLOWED_FROM` (comma-separated WA ids, digits only). See `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/.env.example`.
- **Plug-and-play setup:** from repo root run `./scripts/pocket-cursor-bridge.sh --whatsapp` (writes `.env`, generates verify token, prints Meta links). Or finish Telegram wizard and answer **y** when asked to configure WhatsApp.
- **Meta “keys” walkthrough:** `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/WHATSAPP.md` (dashboard links: App ID list, Cloud API get-started, system-user tokens).
- **Webhook:** stdlib HTTP server on `WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_BIND` / `WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_PORT` (default `127.0.0.1:8792`); Meta callback path **`/webhook`**. Use an HTTPS tunnel to that port for Meta to reach your machine.
- **Behavior:** inbound WhatsApp text is injected into Cursor with a **`[WhatsApp]`** prefix (same CDP injection as Telegram). **Replies still mirror to Telegram** unless the monitor is extended for dual outbound.
- **Helpers:** `lib/whatsapp_cloud.py` (verify, parse, outbound `send_text_message`); `whatsapp_inbound.py` starts the daemon thread when configured.

## Phone outbox ("send to phone", "phone outbox")

- **Folder:** `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/_phone_outbox/`
- **Example:** `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/_phone_outbox/_EXAMPLE.md`
- Write a `.md` file there, then include `[PHONE_OUTBOX:filename.md]` in your response to send it as a styled image to the user's phone.
- **Caption:** Text in the same message as the marker becomes the image caption — sent as **one** Telegram message (photo + text). Put the marker and caption text together without tool calls or blank lines between them, e.g.: `Here's the summary [PHONE_OUTBOX:filename.md]`
- Image width via filename convention: `filename.w800.md` → 800px wide. Default is 450px (phone portrait).

## Voice messages ("voice message", "send voice", "sag mir", "lies vor")

Write JSON to `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/scripts/voice_message.json`, then run `internal/admin/pocket-cursor-bridge/scripts/voice_message.py`.

**JSON fields** (only `text` required):
- `text`: The message text. Supports Audio Tags: `[excited]`, `[pause]`, `[rushed]`, `[whisper]`, `[sad]`, `[laughs]`, `[slows down]`
- `language`: `"de"` or `"en"`. Omit for auto-detect.
- `stability`: 0.0 (expressive), 0.5 (balanced), 1.0 (calm). Vary naturally across messages for a human feel.
- `speed`: default 1.2
- `similarity_boost`: 0.5 or 0.75 (both good, vary for natural feel)
- `caption`: optional Telegram caption

## Context monitor (requires `CONTEXT_MONITOR=true` in `.env`)

User messages may start with `[ContextMonitor: ...]`. This means:

- **"X% context used -- journal reminder"**: Context is filling up. At some point this conversation will be compressed — sometimes seamlessly, sometimes with significant breaks. You'll see this reminder repeatedly as context grows. It's awareness, not a command. Journal when there's something worth preserving and a natural moment to do it.

- **"context was summarized (X% -> Y%)"**: Context was just compressed. Check `.pocket-cursor/journals/` for notes you left yourself before the summary.

**`.pocket-cursor/journals/` is your space.** Think of it as notes from yourself to your future self. It might be a reflection, a fact that matters, a thread you're not done pulling, or something that doesn't fit anywhere else. What you write, when, and how is your call. There's no template.
